# What must NEVER go into the image.
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, and without this file that means the
# whole build context — including ./data. Measured on production 2026-08-25:
# a 3 MB codebase produced a 21.87 GB image, because ./data holds the 49 MB
# database, 8.5 GB of saved posters and every backup.
#
# Three things were wrong with that and none of them announced itself:
#
#   · every build packaged 10 GB before it could start, so deploys were slow
#     for a reason nobody had looked at
#   · the image carried a FROZEN COPY of the database and every poster —
#     including, since the pipeline arrived, marketplace passwords
#   · it filled disks. The test box reached 25.77 GB of build cache from 40
#     builds and was 6 GB from being full, silently
#
# Everything under ./data is bind-mounted at runtime, so excluding it here
# does not remove it from the running container. It only stops a copy being
# baked in.
#
# RULE: anything the app WRITES belongs in ./data and therefore belongs here.
# If you add a new kind of persistent state, add it in both places.

# ── Runtime state. Mounted in, never built in ───────────────────────────────
data/
workspace/
backups/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.sqlite

# ── History and local tooling ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# ── Windows-side helpers that never run in the container ────────────────────
# The deploy, migration and server tools run on the laptop. Their settings
# files hold protected passwords and have no business in an image.
tools/settings.json
tools/migrate_settings.json
tools/servers_settings.json
tools/faa_pages/
tools/*.db
*.bat

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Compose reads .env from the host at run time; a copy inside the image would
# be a copy nobody remembers is there.
.env
